        // But we can simulate prior state by sending Ether to the contract and directly manipulating
        // rewardsForA by calling getFirstWithdrawalBonus on a different recipient that we control is not possible.
        // Instead, we exploit that rewardsForA is private and there's no setter; however the reference
        // property we assert is about preserving prior rewardsForA when external call reverts. We can
        // create that prior by first calling a helper function sequence on the contract: call getFirstWithdrawalBonus
        // for an address that DOES accept funds to set it up, then rely on reverter case to test preservation.

        // Deploy an acceptor contract that will accept the initial withdraw so we can set rewardsForA to boundedPrior
        Acceptor acc = new Acceptor();
        address acceptor = address(acc);

